1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,107
On the morning of April twenty-third,

2
00:00:03,107 --> 00:00:08,480
fourteen fifty-three, the defenders of Constantinople looked down at

3
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:11,520
the one stretch of water they thought was perfectly

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,140
safe…

5
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:16,460
and saw enemy warships floating in it.

6
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:17,760
Dozens of them.

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,300
The harbor was still locked.

8
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:23,120
The great chain was still in place.

9
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:25,320
Nobody had broken through.

10
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,160
So how did the ships get in?

11
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,860
They came over a hill.

12
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:39,330
In fourteen fifty-three, Constantinople was more than a city.

13
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:42,510
For over a thousand years it had been the

14
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:44,710
capital of the Eastern Roman Empire,

15
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:46,350
the Byzantine Empire.

16
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,190
It sat on a triangle of land,

17
00:00:49,190 --> 00:00:50,970
with water on two sides,

18
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:54,130
and the strongest walls of the medieval world on

19
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:54,530
the third.

20
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:58,050
The land walls, built in the fifth century,

21
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:00,070
ran for about six kilometers:

22
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:02,650
a moat, an outer wall,

23
00:01:03,050 --> 00:01:04,670
and a towering inner wall,

24
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:07,030
with nearly two hundred towers.

25
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:11,630
For a thousand years, no army had ever broken

26
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:12,350
through them.

27
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:16,870
But by fourteen fifty-three, the empire around the city

28
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:18,270
was almost gone.

29
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:20,970
What was left was a proud,

30
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:25,350
half-empty capital, surrounded by the rising power of the

31
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:25,850
Ottomans.

32
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,380
The Ottoman sultan was Mehmed the Second.

33
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,060
He was just twenty-one years old,

34
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,720
and he had one goal:

35
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:38,060
to take the city that his ancestors had failed

36
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:38,580
to take.

37
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:41,400
He prepared for it like an engineer.

38
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:44,880
He built a fortress on the Bosphorus to cut

39
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,020
off help from the north.

40
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:49,920
He hired a Hungarian cannon-maker named Orban.

41
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,600
Orban had first offered his services to the Byzantine

42
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,360
emperor, but the emperor couldn't afford him.

43
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:00,060
Mehmed paid him four times what he asked.

44
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:04,820
Orban cast a bronze bombard so huge it needed

45
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,760
dozens of oxen to pull it,

46
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,860
and its stone balls weighed more than half a

47
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:10,160
ton.

48
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:14,460
In early April, he arrived outside the walls with

49
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,960
an army of perhaps eighty thousand men.

50
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:21,120
Inside, the last emperor, Constantine the Eleventh,

51
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,780
had fewer than eight thousand defenders,

52
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,580
among them a band of Genoese soldiers led by

53
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:30,340
a famous captain, Giovanni Giustiniani.

54
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:34,750
The defenders knew where the weak point was.

55
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:39,770
In twelve oh-four, crusaders had captured Constantinople not from

56
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:41,550
the land, but from the harbor,

57
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:45,070
the Golden Horn, where the sea walls were lower

58
00:02:45,070 --> 00:02:45,870
and weaker.

59
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:48,330
So before the Ottomans arrived,

60
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:52,370
the Byzantines stretched an enormous chain across the mouth

61
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,970
of the Golden Horn, from the city to the

62
00:02:54,970 --> 00:02:56,750
tower of Galata on the other side.

63
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:59,090
It floated on wooden logs,

64
00:02:59,610 --> 00:03:01,770
and behind it waited the Christian ships.

65
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,190
As long as the chain held,

66
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,950
the harbor walls didn't need many defenders.

67
00:03:07,570 --> 00:03:10,530
And every soldier saved there could fight on the

68
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:11,110
land walls.

69
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:16,940
Mehmed's cannons pounded the land walls day after day,

70
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:20,500
but every night the defenders rebuilt the damage.

71
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,860
His fleet attacked the chain,

72
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:23,840
and failed.

73
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:29,420
Then, on April twentieth, four Christian ships carrying supplies

74
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:31,980
sailed straight through the Ottoman navy,

75
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,540
in front of the whole city.

76
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:37,200
The sultan was so furious that he rode his

77
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:40,400
horse into the sea, shouting orders at his admiral.

78
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,920
The four ships reached the chain,

79
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:44,480
it was lowered for them,

80
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,240
and they slipped into the harbor.

81
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,040
The siege was two weeks old,

82
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,680
and it was going badly.

83
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:55,750
So Mehmed decided that if his ships couldn't go

84
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:59,010
through the chain, they would go around it.

85
00:03:59,210 --> 00:03:59,970
Over land.

86
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:04,170
Behind the Genoese colony of Galata rose a hill.

87
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:07,070
The Genoese there were officially neutral,

88
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:10,370
trading with both sides, and the Ottomans would pass

89
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:11,970
right outside their walls.

90
00:04:12,870 --> 00:04:15,350
On the other side was the Golden Horn,

91
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:16,910
behind the chain.

92
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:19,990
His men cleared a road over it,

93
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:22,350
laid down wooden rails and rollers,

94
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:24,950
and covered them with fat and oil.

95
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:27,830
The idea wasn't completely new.

96
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:32,050
Only fourteen years earlier, the Venetians had hauled a

97
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:34,710
fleet over the mountains to Lake Garda in Italy.

98
00:04:35,430 --> 00:04:37,430
But no one expected it here,

99
00:04:37,910 --> 00:04:40,310
and certainly not this fast.

100
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:44,680
On the night of April twenty-second,

101
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,060
the operation began.

102
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:49,860
Ships were pulled from the Bosphorus onto cradles,

103
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:53,120
and teams of oxen and men hauled them up

104
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,980
the slope on the greased rollers.

105
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:58,940
According to the chroniclers, the sailors sat at their

106
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:01,040
oars and the sails were raised,

107
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,540
as if the ships were already at sea,

108
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,920
while drums and trumpets played.

109
00:05:06,910 --> 00:05:10,340
By morning, around seventy ships had crossed the hill

110
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:12,540
and slid down into the Golden Horn.

111
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,040
These weren't giant warships.

112
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,060
Most were light galleys and smaller vessels.

113
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,040
But they were enough.

114
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:23,730
The chain had not been broken,

115
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:25,970
but it no longer mattered.

116
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:29,410
Now the defenders had to guard the long sea

117
00:05:29,410 --> 00:05:32,550
walls along the harbor, and pull men away from

118
00:05:32,550 --> 00:05:35,130
the land walls, where they were desperately needed.

119
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:39,450
On April twenty-eighth, the Venetians tried to burn the

120
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:41,410
new Ottoman fleet in a night raid.

121
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,690
The Ottomans had been warned.

122
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:47,270
The attack failed, and the lead ship was sunk.

123
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:51,550
Soon the Ottomans built a floating bridge across the

124
00:05:51,550 --> 00:05:54,910
Golden Horn, letting troops and cannons reach the harbor

125
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:55,350
walls.

126
00:05:56,250 --> 00:05:59,390
The city was now under pressure from almost every

127
00:05:59,390 --> 00:05:59,790
side.

128
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:04,113
Before dawn on May twenty-ninth,

129
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:08,420
fourteen fifty-three, after nearly two months of siege,

130
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,500
the Ottomans launched their final assault.

131
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,460
For hours the defenders held.

132
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,940
Then Giustiniani was badly wounded and carried from the

133
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:19,200
walls.

134
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,740
According to one famous story,

135
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:25,140
a small gate called the Kerkoporta had been left

136
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:28,060
open, and Ottoman soldiers slipped through.

137
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:32,760
The defense broke, and the last Byzantine emperor died

138
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,040
fighting at the walls.

139
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,380
Constantinople fell.

140
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:39,860
More than a thousand years of Roman rule in

141
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:41,440
the east came to an end,

142
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:44,500
and the city became the new Ottoman capital:

143
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:45,560
Istanbul.

144
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,300
The ships that crossed the hill didn't win the

145
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,200
siege by themselves.

146
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:52,180
But in a single night,

147
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:55,580
they turned an impossible wall of water into just

148
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:59,760
another front, and showed what a twenty-one-year-old sultan was

149
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:00,700
willing to try.

